N1  - The mean duration of pain for the exercise therapy group was <12 weeks. Additionally, the contribution of SMT to the treatment effect could not be discerned. The aim of this study was to compare the effect of manual therapy, including specific exercises and segmental techniques to general exercise therapy in chronic LBP patients. In the manual therapy group, the patients also performed a subset of five general exercises for the spine, abdomen, and lower limbs, and six specific and localized exercises for spinal segments and the pelvic girdle in each treatment session in order to normalize function. This trial was also identified in the European Guidelines for the Management of Chronic Low-back pain (European Spine Journal 2006; 15(supplement 2): see p. S241; also available from http://www.backpaineurope.org/web/files/WG2_Guidelines.pdf ), and also excluded for the same reason.
